          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "For that I'll go to this meals folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "and then there this dynamic segment folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "this mealSlug folder, and then there this page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 16.02,
          "en": "because that is the component responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.02,
          "end": 18.453,
          "en": "for outputting the details about a meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 22.38,
          "en": "Now here I again then want to output a fragment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.38,
          "end": 23.88,
          "en": "because I want to have a header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 26.1,
          "en": "and next to that the main section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.1,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "as we had it on many other pages as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "Now, I also prepared some styles for this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 35.13,
          "en": "So attached you find a page.module.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.13,
          "end": 38.163,
          "en": "which you should store next to this page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "And then we can import our classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 45.76,
          "en": "from that page.module.css file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.48,
          "end": 51.84,
          "en": "so that then we can, for example, add a class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 55.833,
          "en": "to this header, a class named header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.69,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "In that header, I then want to have a couple of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 64.83,
          "en": "For example, I wanna have a div in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.83,
          "end": 69.09,
          "en": "with a class of image, which will then be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.09,
          "end": 73.77,
          "en": "for outputting the meal image that belongs to a meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.77,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "And we will output that image with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "of the image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 80.43,
          "en": "which is provided by NextJS imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 82.473,
          "en": "from the next/image package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84,
          "end": 86.13,
          "en": "Now we'll configure this image later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.13,
          "end": 89.25,
          "en": "because at the moment we don't have the meal yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.25,
          "end": 91.65,
          "en": "We'll add the logic for that soon though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.65,
          "end": 95.72999999999999,
          "en": "The only thing I want to add already is this fill prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 98.97,
          "en": "since again, I won't know the exact dimensions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.97,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "of the image file yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.47,
          "end": 103.8,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll use this fill prop as a fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.8,
          "end": 105.18299999999999,
          "en": "or as a solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "Then below that, I'll add another div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 113.53999999999999,
          "en": "with a class of headerText,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 122.49,
          "en": "written like this, not with a dash, but instead camel case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.49,
          "end": 127.05,
          "en": "That's how the CSS class name in the CSS file is named.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.05,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "In there, you should then add a h1 element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "where we'll later output the meal title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 135.27,
          "en": "And below that a paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.27,
          "end": 139.98,
          "en": "which receives another CSS class, a class of creator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.98,
          "end": 142.71,
          "en": "where I want to output the text by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.71,
          "end": 147.48,
          "en": "and then the name of the creator wrapped into a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.48,
          "end": 150.21,
          "en": "And here I'll use the regular anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.21,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "because this should actually be a link that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 155.763,
          "en": "to send an email to that creator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "Therefore, the actual href value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 162.93,
          "en": "will be a dynamically generated string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.93,
          "end": 165.24,
          "en": "using this string literal syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.24,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "with those backticks here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 168.663,
          "en": "where I'll say mailto:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.59,
          "end": 171.57,
          "en": "and then here I'll inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.57,
          "end": 174.84300000000002,
          "en": "that email address once we have it later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.7,
          "end": 178.2,
          "en": "And that's how we can set up a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 180,
          "en": "that will open the Mail program,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 183.243,
          "en": "so that users can send an email to that person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.07,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "Below that, we can add another paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 190.05,
          "en": "which also receives a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.05,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "and here the class should be the summary class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 196.29,
          "en": "where I want to output the short summary text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.29,
          "end": 197.793,
          "en": "that summarizes a meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.365,
          "end": 201.45,
          "en": "And that's then this header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.45,
          "end": 203.22,
          "en": "Of course, a lot of data is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 204.903,
          "en": "but we'll take care of that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.97,
          "end": 208.92000000000002,
          "en": "Now in that main section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.92000000000002,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "I simply wanna output one paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 215.94299999999998,
          "en": "which receives a CSS class name called instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.02,
          "end": 220.92000000000002,
          "en": "And then here, I want to output the instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.92000000000002,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "that are stored for every meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 227.52,
          "en": "And those should actually be output as HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.52,
          "end": 229.71,
          "en": "which can be achieved in React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.71,
          "end": 234.71,
          "en": "by targeting the dangerouslySetInnerHTML prop on an element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.85,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "And it's called like this because you open yourself up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 244.44,
          "en": "to cross-site scripting attacks when outputting content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.44,
          "end": 248.103,
          "en": "as HTML content, at least if you're not validating it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.39,
          "end": 253.08,
          "en": "Now this prop then wants a object as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.08,
          "end": 258.08,
          "en": "and that object should have an __html property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 261.48,
          "en": "which then contains the actual HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.48,
          "end": 263.82,
          "en": "that should be output on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.82,
          "end": 265.38,
          "en": "Now we'll get that code later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.38,
          "end": 267.12,
          "en": "from that meal once we fetched it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.12,
          "end": 269.37,
          "en": "but that's how we'll output it on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.01,
          "end": 275.97,
          "en": "So that this is in the end our Meal Details page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.97,
          "end": 278.94,
          "en": "without the data that we wanna output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.94,
          "end": 280.92,
          "en": "Now, in order to have some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.92,
          "end": 283.08,
          "en": "to output on that Meal Detail screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 286.443,
          "en": "we should go back to the meals.js file in the lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.4,
          "end": 290.88,
          "en": "and there we can export another async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.88,
          "end": 292.773,
          "en": "that could be called getMeal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.88,
          "end": 297.51,
          "en": "And here I then expect to get the slug of the meal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.51,
          "end": 300.483,
          "en": "that identifies the meal that should be fetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.35,
          "end": 306.03,
          "en": "Well, and then we simply wanna return db.prepare,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.03,
          "end": 311.03,
          "en": "and then SELECT all columns FROM the meals table",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.49,
          "end": 314.01,
          "en": "WHERE the slug field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.01,
          "end": 316.503,
          "en": "is equal to the slug we're getting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 318.21,
          "end": 321.06,
          "en": "Now you could now add it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 321.06,
          "end": 323.04,
          "en": "but that would be insecure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 323.04,
          "end": 325.863,
          "en": "That opens yourself up to SQL injection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 326.76,
          "end": 328.98,
          "en": "Instead, you should use a question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.98,
          "end": 331.17,
          "en": "as a placeholder here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.17,
          "end": 333.93,
          "en": "and then call the get method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.93,
          "end": 336.453,
          "en": "since I only want to get a single record,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.62,
          "end": 340.71,
          "en": "and then you pass the value that should be inserted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.71,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "for that placeholder to get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 347.58,
          "en": "In this case that's slug, which we get here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 347.58,
          "end": 351.213,
          "en": "Under the hood, this better-sqlite3 package we're using here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.213,
          "end": 355.11,
          "en": "will then protect you against SQL injection attacks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.11,
          "end": 357.48,
          "en": "That's why you should add dynamic values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.48,
          "end": 360.03,
          "en": "into your statements like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.03,
          "end": 362.463,
          "en": "So that should then return a meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.75,
          "end": 368.013,
          "en": "So we can therefore go back to this Meals Detail page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 368.91,
          "end": 371.86,
          "en": "and now in there, call getMeal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 374.25,
          "end": 376.41,
          "en": "and import that from that lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 376.41,
          "end": 377.973,
          "en": "and the meals.js file there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 380.821,
          "end": 382.53,
          "en": "Here, we'll then get back a meal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 382.53,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "which we can then use down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 387.363,
          "en": "to well populate this JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 388.32,
          "end": 391.353,
          "en": "but getMeal of course needs that slug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 392.22,
          "end": 397.22,
          "en": "And that slug is simply that part that's encoded in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 397.68,
          "end": 400.47,
          "en": "that is caught with help of this placeholder here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 400.47,
          "end": 402.243,
          "en": "this mealSlug placeholder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 403.29,
          "end": 406.62,
          "en": "So how do we then get access to that concrete value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 406.62,
          "end": 408.273,
          "en": "that's part of the URL?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 409.32,
          "end": 412.98,
          "en": "With help of the props we are receiving on this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 412.98,
          "end": 417.36,
          "en": "I mentioned before that NextJS is passing some special props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 417.36,
          "end": 419.34000000000003,
          "en": "to these special files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 419.34000000000003,
          "end": 423.15,
          "en": "or to these components in those special files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 423.15,
          "end": 425.34,
          "en": "And for example, every component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 425.34,
          "end": 428.28,
          "en": "that's stored in a page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 428.28,
          "end": 431.16,
          "en": "will receive a special params prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 431.16,
          "end": 434.395,
          "en": "which you can, therefore, destructure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 434.395,
          "end": 438.48,
          "en": "And this params prop will then itself contain an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 438.48,
